1
00:00:05,689 --> 00:00:09,659
Heiwa Fansubs Presents:
"Great Detective Conan"
"Challenge to Kudo Shin'ichi"

2
00:00:10,427 --> 00:00:12,262
I know now.

3
00:00:12,829 --> 00:00:16,033
Just why we are trapped in this room.

4
00:00:17,701 --> 00:00:19,870
The criminal who did all this...

5
00:00:21,838 --> 00:00:23,373
Ran...

6
00:00:23,673 --> 00:00:25,375
...it was you.

7
00:00:36,686 --> 00:00:39,056
That's right, Shin'ichi.

8
00:00:48,298 --> 00:00:50,400
Truth is, I...

9
00:00:57,340 --> 00:00:59,309
Ran! Are you okay?!

10
00:00:59,543 --> 00:01:01,111
Shin'ichi?!

11
00:01:03,146 --> 00:01:04,781
Damn!

12
00:01:16,059 --> 00:01:17,260
Shin'ichi.

13
00:01:17,527 --> 00:01:20,464
What is this?

14
00:01:21,398 --> 00:01:22,933
Some gas...

15
00:01:25,902 --> 00:01:27,504
Shin'ichi...

16
00:01:39,449 --> 00:01:40,817
Ran...

17
00:01:53,730 --> 00:01:55,665
Kudo-kun, Kudo-kun.

18
00:01:55,765 --> 00:01:56,867
Are you hurt anywhere?

19
00:01:56,967 --> 00:01:58,802
"High School Student Detective
Kudo Shin'ichi"

20
00:01:58,902 --> 00:02:00,070
Kudo-kun.

21
00:02:00,871 --> 00:02:02,672
"MPD Investigation Unit One
Takagi Wataru"

22
00:02:02,739 --> 00:02:04,341
Thank goodness.

23
00:02:04,808 --> 00:02:07,210
Sato-san, Kudo-kun has
recovered consciousness.

24
00:02:07,244 --> 00:02:08,445
"MPD Investigation Unit One
Sato Miwako"

25
00:02:08,512 --> 00:02:12,048
Both of them were found collapsed.
They're being identified right now.

26
00:02:12,616 --> 00:02:14,818
"Shin'ichi's Childhood Friend
Mori Ran"

27
00:02:15,819 --> 00:02:16,820
Ran...

28
00:02:16,920 --> 00:02:18,388
Ran! Are you okay?

29
00:02:18,455 --> 00:02:20,056
Please don't over strain yourself.

30
00:02:20,190 --> 00:02:21,558
I'm fine.

31
00:02:21,725 --> 00:02:25,729
Um... Could it be that Ran's been injured?

32
00:02:27,764 --> 00:02:30,667
I'm sorry, but... she's dead.

33
00:02:30,867 --> 00:02:32,169
Huh?

34
00:02:32,402 --> 00:02:34,171
"Medical Coroner - Hirata Hajime"
For the moment, the cause of death is unknown.

35
00:02:34,471 --> 00:02:37,340
After an autopsy,
I think we'll find out something.

36
00:02:37,440 --> 00:02:39,342
Right away, please.

37
00:02:39,709 --> 00:02:41,344
Understood.

38
00:02:42,379 --> 00:02:44,948
Wait... Hold on a minute!

39
00:02:45,048 --> 00:02:47,184
Please wait a minute!

40
00:02:47,551 --> 00:02:50,987
Kudo-kun, do you remember who I am?

41
00:02:51,087 --> 00:02:55,058
Truth is, you and I met once before
at a crime scene.

42
00:02:55,158 --> 00:02:57,561
What are you talking about at a time like this?!
More importantly, Ran!

43
00:02:57,594 --> 00:03:00,263
Her body has already gotten cold.

44
00:03:00,530 --> 00:03:07,404
It's regrettable you and I had to
meet again in this way, isn't it?

45
00:03:09,272 --> 00:03:10,373
If you would please.

46
00:03:10,473 --> 00:03:11,775
Please wait!

47
00:03:11,841 --> 00:03:13,009
- Ran!
- Calm down!

48
00:03:13,076 --> 00:03:14,444
Ran!

49
00:03:15,879 --> 00:03:17,547
Kudo-kun! Calm down.

50
00:03:17,614 --> 00:03:19,549
I understand how you feel, Kudo-kun.
I understand, but...

51
00:03:19,649 --> 00:03:21,251
Kudo-kun!

52
00:03:21,384 --> 00:03:26,990
What you can do for Ran right now
is tell us everything you know!

53
00:03:27,190 --> 00:03:28,458
Let me go!

54
00:03:28,558 --> 00:03:30,860
- Come to the station with us.
- Lemme go!

55
00:03:30,961 --> 00:03:32,429
Ran!

56
00:03:32,929 --> 00:03:34,431
Ran!

57
00:03:39,436 --> 00:03:42,005
Raaan!

58
00:03:51,448 --> 00:03:54,084
"Beika West Police Station"
Were there any suspicious points
at the crime scene?

59
00:03:54,184 --> 00:03:55,652
Crime scene?

60
00:03:56,052 --> 00:03:58,188
The place where Ran and I collapsed.

61
00:03:58,288 --> 00:04:03,460
That reminds me, the ground around where Ran
had collapsed was a little wet, wasn't it?

62
00:04:03,627 --> 00:04:04,728
Wet?

63
00:04:04,761 --> 00:04:07,564
Kudo-kun, you haven't told us anything...

64
00:04:07,831 --> 00:04:13,203
...but I think you two were carried there from
somewhere else after you had lost consciousness.

65
00:04:14,104 --> 00:04:19,175
That's why Ran-chan was
the only one who was wet, right?

66
00:04:19,409 --> 00:04:24,547
But the condition of the corpse
doesn't match that of someone who had drowned.

67
00:04:27,284 --> 00:04:29,019
Are you okay, Kudo-kun?
Kudo-kun!

68
00:04:29,085 --> 00:04:31,755
You should go to the restroom.
Kudo-kun, this way.

69
00:04:38,128 --> 00:04:41,731
At any rate, for Ran-kun's sake,
we'll investigate this with all our might.

70
00:04:44,501 --> 00:04:46,369
That's why, Kudo-kun...

71
00:04:47,971 --> 00:04:52,075
...you should place your trust in
Sato-san and myself...

72
00:04:52,676 --> 00:04:56,880
...and we hope your deposition
will advance our investigation.

73
00:04:56,913 --> 00:04:58,882
"How disappointing, Great Detective, you forgot
something important at the scene of the crime"

74
00:04:59,149 --> 00:05:01,551
"You forgot something at the scene of the crime"
Because you're a major witness...

75
00:05:01,718 --> 00:05:04,954
...there may be police officers in here
who will say unpleasant things to you...

76
00:05:05,188 --> 00:05:07,257
...but I want you to overlook it.

77
00:05:08,925 --> 00:05:10,393
Whaa! Hey!

78
00:05:10,560 --> 00:05:12,996
Watch it there, Kudo-kun.

79
00:05:13,063 --> 00:05:14,464
I'm sorry.

80
00:05:16,132 --> 00:05:18,735
Truth is, Kudo-kun, Sato-san and I...

81
00:05:20,136 --> 00:05:21,571
Kudo-kun?

82
00:05:25,241 --> 00:05:26,710
Kudo-kun!

83
00:05:27,677 --> 00:05:29,245
Kudo-kun!

84
00:05:30,046 --> 00:05:31,247
Kudo-kun!

85
00:05:31,448 --> 00:05:32,649
Kudo-kun!

86
00:05:33,049 --> 00:05:36,319
Sato-san!
Kudo-kun has run off!

87
00:05:36,453 --> 00:05:38,822
The major witness in
a murder case has escaped!

88
00:05:38,888 --> 00:05:42,392
To repeat! The major witness in
a murder case has escaped!

89
00:05:42,492 --> 00:05:44,394
Block all major arterial roads...

90
00:05:54,904 --> 00:05:56,139
"Shin'ichi and Ran's Fellow Student
Suzuki Sonoko"

91
00:05:56,172 --> 00:05:58,842
Kudo-kun, what's wrong?

92
00:05:58,908 --> 00:06:01,845
What is it? Have you
gotten involved in a case again?

93
00:06:02,312 --> 00:06:05,115
That's right.
Sonoko, I need a favor from you.

94
00:06:05,382 --> 00:06:09,986
Without asking me anything,
could you take me to the Beika Marina?

95
00:06:11,121 --> 00:06:12,889
Please.

96
00:06:18,228 --> 00:06:22,065
Could it be Kudo-kun,
you're being chased by the police?

97
00:06:23,533 --> 00:06:25,902
Please, help me.
Please trust me.

98
00:06:28,538 --> 00:06:30,073
Leave it to me.

99
00:06:31,074 --> 00:06:32,075
"Beika Marina"

100
00:06:32,142 --> 00:06:34,511
I don't know what case
you've gotten yourself involved in...

101
00:06:34,611 --> 00:06:37,647
...but once it's settled,
explain it all to me, okay?

102
00:06:37,881 --> 00:06:40,150
Yeah. Thank you.

103
00:06:56,099 --> 00:06:57,434
"How disappointing, Great Detective, you forgot
something important at the scene of the crime"

104
00:06:57,500 --> 00:06:59,702
"What is it I forgot?"

105
00:07:02,138 --> 00:07:06,609
"This note was clearly put into
my pocket by the criminal."

106
00:07:06,943 --> 00:07:10,980
"What on earth is the criminal's goal?"

107
00:07:16,219 --> 00:07:17,320
Ran...!

108
00:07:20,690 --> 00:07:21,958
Damn...!

109
00:07:22,025 --> 00:07:23,960
What is this about!?

110
00:07:29,933 --> 00:07:31,234
"Private Detective
Mori Kogoro"

111
00:07:31,301 --> 00:07:34,170
Fool! It's me, I tell you!
Stop that you fool! It's me!

112
00:07:34,304 --> 00:07:36,172
Sorry! Sir, are you okay?!

113
00:07:38,942 --> 00:07:42,011
Sir, how did you get out of the white room?

114
00:07:42,312 --> 00:07:43,713
Well, I dunno.

115
00:07:43,780 --> 00:07:45,815
I lost consciousness about that time.

116
00:07:46,015 --> 00:07:49,552
When I came to, I was sleeping on
a bench in some strange park.

117
00:07:49,686 --> 00:07:53,256
And, while there, a letter was left behind
telling me to come and meet you here.

118
00:07:53,323 --> 00:07:54,090
"Mori Ran and Kudo Shin'ichi
are at Beika Marina"

119
00:07:54,123 --> 00:07:57,694
But there were a lot of police around...

120
00:08:02,098 --> 00:08:03,433
Oi...

121
00:08:05,235 --> 00:08:06,803
It's a lie, right?

122
00:08:09,606 --> 00:08:13,877
It's absolutely a lie that Ran is dead, right!

123
00:08:16,412 --> 00:08:18,248
My daughter is...

124
00:08:21,150 --> 00:08:24,821
Oi, tell me that it's a lie!

125
00:08:27,757 --> 00:08:29,893
She's only 17!

126
00:08:31,828 --> 00:08:35,365
What would my 17 year old daughter die from?!

127
00:08:35,698 --> 00:08:37,100
Why?!

128
00:08:40,970 --> 00:08:42,906
Answer me, boy detective!

129
00:08:46,409 --> 00:08:47,577
That's!?

130
00:08:49,479 --> 00:08:51,014
What is it?!

131
00:08:53,483 --> 00:08:55,451
Ran's cell phone!

132
00:08:55,585 --> 00:08:56,753
Ran's?!

133
00:08:57,720 --> 00:08:59,289
It's cold...

134
00:09:01,057 --> 00:09:04,627
That reminds me, that glass was clouded.

135
00:09:04,727 --> 00:09:08,298
"The ground where Ran had collapsed
was a little wet, wasn't it?"

136
00:09:08,364 --> 00:09:10,433
The ground was wet...

137
00:09:10,633 --> 00:09:12,101
Cloudy...

138
00:09:12,168 --> 00:09:13,903
A temperature difference...

139
00:09:14,003 --> 00:09:16,205
A frozen cell phone!

140
00:09:16,573 --> 00:09:18,608
Ran was wet.

141
00:09:20,109 --> 00:09:23,079
I've got it! Flash-freezing!

142
00:09:23,379 --> 00:09:27,250
The criminal in that white room
only flash-froze the room Ran was in!

143
00:09:27,317 --> 00:09:29,586
It may be that Ran is still alive!

144
00:09:29,719 --> 00:09:31,054
Eh?!

145
00:09:31,120 --> 00:09:33,456
I've read about a state of
apparent death due to flash-freezing...

146
00:09:33,590 --> 00:09:36,993
...that was researched in the past
all around the world.

147
00:09:37,260 --> 00:09:39,696
They seemingly really had died...

148
00:09:39,796 --> 00:09:43,466
...but when defrosted properly,
there were cases where they were revived.

149
00:09:43,533 --> 00:09:46,970
Is that true!
Is it true Ran really is alive?!

150
00:09:54,243 --> 00:09:55,645
"The True Criminal"

151
00:09:58,748 --> 00:10:00,083
Hello...

152
00:10:00,249 --> 00:10:04,621
Kudo Shin'ichi, I shall give you
one piece of information.

153
00:10:04,988 --> 00:10:06,889
Who are you!?
What on earth is your goal?!

154
00:10:06,956 --> 00:10:09,092
Mori Ran's autopsy...

155
00:10:09,359 --> 00:10:12,462
...has been set for today at 16:00.

156
00:10:12,595 --> 00:10:13,730
Eh!?

157
00:10:13,830 --> 00:10:16,099
That's one hour from now.

158
00:10:16,299 --> 00:10:20,169
Can you get your love back
with your own hand?

159
00:10:28,244 --> 00:10:29,479
Autopsy?!

160
00:10:29,646 --> 00:10:31,814
They're going to do an autopsy
on Ran even though she's alive?!

161
00:10:31,948 --> 00:10:33,516
Sir, let's hurry!

162
00:10:33,583 --> 00:10:34,717
Yeah!

163
00:10:34,884 --> 00:10:38,054
"Beika West Police Station
Morgue"

164
00:10:51,200 --> 00:10:53,002
"Beika West Police Station"

165
00:10:58,374 --> 00:11:03,913
Excuse me, I caught this boy shoplifting
at Beika Bookstore, so I've brought him in.

166
00:11:04,047 --> 00:11:05,982
Which floor is your
person in charge of thefts?

167
00:11:06,082 --> 00:11:07,650
I'm sorry! I repent it!

168
00:11:07,717 --> 00:11:08,918
You should repent!

169
00:11:08,985 --> 00:11:10,787
In that case, it's on the 2nd floor.

170
00:11:10,953 --> 00:11:12,388
Thank you!

171
00:11:12,722 --> 00:11:14,257
Wait!

172
00:11:15,758 --> 00:11:17,360
What is it?

173
00:11:19,328 --> 00:11:22,732
I want to ask you something about
the security here. Is that okay?

174
00:11:23,566 --> 00:11:25,201
Your mother is crying, you know!

175
00:11:25,268 --> 00:11:26,769
I'm sorry!

176
00:11:32,975 --> 00:11:34,377
Good job.

177
00:11:40,049 --> 00:11:41,584
"Morgue"
Sir!

178
00:11:49,158 --> 00:11:50,893
- Ran...!
- Ran!

179
00:11:55,732 --> 00:11:56,933
Ran!

180
00:11:57,233 --> 00:11:58,468
Ran...

181
00:11:58,601 --> 00:11:59,802
Ran!

182
00:11:59,836 --> 00:12:01,571
- Sir!
- Yeah!

183
00:12:02,872 --> 00:12:04,741
One, two...!

184
00:12:07,043 --> 00:12:08,878
One, two!

185
00:12:10,113 --> 00:12:11,414
Damn!

186
00:12:19,222 --> 00:12:22,158
Calm down!
What happened on May 15th?

187
00:12:23,159 --> 00:12:26,629
Oi! What kind of case was this one?

188
00:12:27,764 --> 00:12:32,235
The murder case that took place in a cold storage
warehouse of a home-delivery company.

189
00:12:32,535 --> 00:12:35,238
"The Medical Examiner's
investigation was wrong."

190
00:12:35,438 --> 00:12:39,976
"This person was accidentally locked in the cold
storage warehouse, but didn't die by freezing."

191
00:12:40,109 --> 00:12:45,114
"They had been brought to
this warehouse and then murdered."

192
00:12:45,281 --> 00:12:46,783
"This is..."

193
00:12:47,316 --> 00:12:49,685
"...a full-fledged murder case."

194
00:12:49,786 --> 00:12:52,288
Ah, it was that case, huh?

195
00:12:52,488 --> 00:12:55,591
But, I don't know what
the 6 character keyword is.

196
00:12:58,327 --> 00:12:59,328
Ah!

197
00:12:59,428 --> 00:13:03,666
"Kudo-kun.
Do you remember who I am?"

198
00:13:05,501 --> 00:13:09,539
Sir! Do you know the name of
the Medical Examiner from that time?

199
00:13:10,506 --> 00:13:11,908
If I recall...

200
00:13:12,041 --> 00:13:14,844
"The Medical Examiner's
investigation was wrong."

201
00:13:14,977 --> 00:13:18,147
"I thought as much myself."

202
00:13:18,447 --> 00:13:20,316
Wasn't it Hirata?

203
00:13:20,650 --> 00:13:24,921
He was this hugely self-confident Medical Examiner
I had met several times at case crime scenes.

204
00:13:25,221 --> 00:13:26,322
Hirata...

205
00:13:26,489 --> 00:13:29,458
That's right!
It was Hirata Hajime!

206
00:13:32,328 --> 00:13:34,330
"Hirata Hajime"

207
00:13:42,538 --> 00:13:43,873
Ran!

208
00:13:44,207 --> 00:13:45,608
No, you're wrong...

209
00:13:45,708 --> 00:13:47,276
This is a mannequin!

210
00:13:47,476 --> 00:13:49,212
Damn!

211
00:13:52,682 --> 00:13:54,417
Stop messing around!

212
00:13:55,651 --> 00:13:56,919
What is this?!

213
00:13:57,153 --> 00:13:59,288
What on earth is this?!

214
00:13:59,455 --> 00:14:02,258
This is your fault, boy detective!

215
00:14:02,625 --> 00:14:06,662
Though you were so concerned about her,
why didn't you protect Ran!

216
00:14:08,130 --> 00:14:10,199
I'm sorry, Sir.

217
00:14:10,666 --> 00:14:13,970
Before saying "sorry," hurry and find Ran!

218
00:14:14,103 --> 00:14:15,938
You're useless!

219
00:14:16,339 --> 00:14:18,374
I'll beat you to death!

220
00:14:18,507 --> 00:14:20,276
Ran!!

221
00:14:34,957 --> 00:14:36,459
What are you doing here?!

222
00:14:36,759 --> 00:14:39,195
This is off-limits to outsiders!

223
00:14:39,595 --> 00:14:42,431
I'll call for a police officer.
Don't move from there.

224
00:14:45,001 --> 00:14:46,068
Huh?

225
00:14:47,770 --> 00:14:51,107
Aren't you Kudo Shin'ichi-kun?

226
00:14:51,540 --> 00:14:55,578
Why would a major witness to
a crime come running off to here?

227
00:14:59,348 --> 00:15:00,850
What is it?

228
00:15:01,484 --> 00:15:04,020
How did you know that we were here?

229
00:15:04,153 --> 00:15:05,588
What are you saying?

230
00:15:05,821 --> 00:15:09,659
After that huge fuss you made,
anyone would have noticed you.

231
00:15:09,859 --> 00:15:12,795
Shouting out "I'll beat you to death"
like that in a police station.

232
00:15:15,097 --> 00:15:16,132
What is it?

233
00:15:16,299 --> 00:15:21,237
Well, because the keyword for
the final panel was your name.

234
00:15:21,437 --> 00:15:22,905
Keyword?

235
00:15:23,105 --> 00:15:24,507
What are you talking about?

236
00:15:24,674 --> 00:15:26,375
I just happened to hear your uproar and...

237
00:15:26,442 --> 00:15:29,679
We were just doing this.

238
00:15:31,414 --> 00:15:33,316
"This is your fault. I'll beat you to death."

239
00:15:33,349 --> 00:15:37,853
It's just I couldn't help but think that
from the wiretap device on this strap...

240
00:15:38,020 --> 00:15:40,489
...we were being watched over by
the one involved in this.

241
00:15:40,589 --> 00:15:42,692
"Sorry, Sir."

242
00:15:42,825 --> 00:15:46,395
"Before saying 'sorry,' hurry and find Ran!"

243
00:15:46,462 --> 00:15:48,631
"You're useless!"

244
00:15:48,831 --> 00:15:50,633
"I'll beat you to death!"

245
00:15:50,866 --> 00:15:52,368
"Ran!!"

246
00:15:54,370 --> 00:15:57,540
When we found Ran's cell phone at that spot...

247
00:15:57,640 --> 00:16:01,744
...I noticed that this part of
the strap had a small hole in it.

248
00:16:02,011 --> 00:16:03,045
That's why we...

249
00:16:03,112 --> 00:16:07,149
"Can you get your love back
with your own hand?"

250
00:16:12,588 --> 00:16:13,622
"Oi!"

251
00:16:13,723 --> 00:16:15,324
"Shh!"

252
00:16:15,491 --> 00:16:16,659
"What's going on?"

253
00:16:16,759 --> 00:16:19,829
"A wiretap has been prepared in this strap."

254
00:16:20,529 --> 00:16:24,300
"Let's take advantage of the fact that
someone is eavesdropping on us, Sir."

255
00:16:27,636 --> 00:16:29,038
"Autopsy!?"

256
00:16:29,138 --> 00:16:31,207
"They're going to do an autopsy on Ran
even though she's alive?!"

257
00:16:31,374 --> 00:16:34,010
- "Sir, let's hurry!"
- "Yeah!"

258
00:16:34,577 --> 00:16:38,981
We deliberately said we were going to
the Morgue so that you would hear it.

259
00:16:39,915 --> 00:16:42,018
And, before coming to this police station...

260
00:16:42,151 --> 00:16:46,956
...the boy detective and I
recorded a fight scene between us.

261
00:16:47,890 --> 00:16:51,227
The criminal who shut us in that white room...

262
00:16:52,061 --> 00:16:54,096
...was you, wasn't it?

263
00:16:56,599 --> 00:16:59,068
Medical Examiner, Hirata Hajime-san.

264
00:17:04,473 --> 00:17:07,777
The criminal who shut us in that white room...

265
00:17:08,644 --> 00:17:10,646
...was you, wasn't it?

266
00:17:11,447 --> 00:17:13,916
Medical Examiner, Hirata Hajime-san.

267
00:17:20,923 --> 00:17:23,726
Why are you talking so triumphantly for?

268
00:17:24,260 --> 00:17:27,263
The situation hasn't changed in the least.

269
00:17:28,631 --> 00:17:31,600
To keep a person in a state of
apparent death by hypothermia...

270
00:17:31,734 --> 00:17:35,704
...it's essential to have a
delicate control over their temperature.

271
00:17:36,272 --> 00:17:40,976
When I press this button,
that temperature control will be suspended.

272
00:17:41,343 --> 00:17:45,948
Then, somewhere in this room,
Mori Ran will die, just as she is.

273
00:17:47,116 --> 00:17:49,885
Yes, yes, that's right, Kudo Shin'ichi.

274
00:17:50,119 --> 00:17:52,388
That's the expression I wanted to see.

275
00:17:52,555 --> 00:17:57,426
That look of misery when
you knew you had lost.

276
00:18:00,329 --> 00:18:03,165
When I met you in town a short while ago...

277
00:18:03,666 --> 00:18:06,368
...you didn't even remember me.

278
00:18:07,036 --> 00:18:12,141
You didn't know at all the times
your voice has run through my thoughts.

279
00:18:12,808 --> 00:18:14,910
Despite appearances...

280
00:18:15,811 --> 00:18:21,217
...I'd been told I was certain to be made next President
of Tokyo's Health Sciences University as an elite doctor.

281
00:18:21,817 --> 00:18:27,156
I had also contributed to cases as
a Medical Examiner, which had led to arrests.

282
00:18:28,157 --> 00:18:29,625
However...

283
00:18:30,526 --> 00:18:33,195
...due to that cold-storage warehouse case...

284
00:18:33,662 --> 00:18:36,899
...both my career and honor
were completely ruined.

285
00:18:39,435 --> 00:18:40,803
Do you understand?

286
00:18:40,970 --> 00:18:44,206
It's your fault my life went out of whack!

287
00:18:44,473 --> 00:18:46,842
That's why you prepared that white room...

288
00:18:47,009 --> 00:18:49,812
...and made me recall those cases from my past.

289
00:18:50,012 --> 00:18:52,515
Since you had torn up people's lives...

290
00:18:52,848 --> 00:18:57,386
...I thought it simple courtesy that you
should at least remember their names and faces.

291
00:18:58,420 --> 00:18:59,922
Save Ran!

292
00:19:00,022 --> 00:19:01,924
Where is Ran?!

293
00:19:02,491 --> 00:19:04,460
"Please" save her, isn't it?

294
00:19:04,727 --> 00:19:06,562
Use respectful language.

295
00:19:06,862 --> 00:19:09,098
Do you understand the position you're in?

296
00:19:09,398 --> 00:19:10,766
Damn...

297
00:19:11,901 --> 00:19:13,869
Oi! Boy detective!

298
00:19:14,170 --> 00:19:16,372
Don't you have any tricks up your sleeve?

299
00:19:19,208 --> 00:19:20,509
No.

300
00:19:20,743 --> 00:19:22,511
Oi!

301
00:19:24,146 --> 00:19:25,814
Hirata-san...

302
00:19:27,316 --> 00:19:29,418
This is my total loss.

303
00:19:30,252 --> 00:19:32,855
So please tell me just one final thing.

304
00:19:34,290 --> 00:19:36,158
How did you...

305
00:19:36,592 --> 00:19:39,295
...shut us into that white room?

306
00:19:39,828 --> 00:19:41,297
What's that...?

307
00:19:41,530 --> 00:19:43,766
If you'd like to know,
then get on your knees and beg!

308
00:19:43,999 --> 00:19:48,270
Say, "I would please like to know, Hirata-san."

309
00:20:02,718 --> 00:20:04,820
I want to know...

310
00:20:05,821 --> 00:20:07,523
Hirata-san...

311
00:20:11,126 --> 00:20:12,861
...please...

312
00:20:14,830 --> 00:20:16,899
...please tell me!

313
00:20:24,940 --> 00:20:28,244
Can't be helped, huh?
Then I'll tell you.

314
00:20:28,577 --> 00:20:33,148
That girlfriend of yours that
you have such total trust in...

315
00:20:33,549 --> 00:20:36,552
...she gave each of you some sleeping pills.

316
00:20:38,387 --> 00:20:39,622
Ran...

317
00:20:39,989 --> 00:20:41,624
She gave them to us?!

318
00:20:43,525 --> 00:20:45,060
Ran...

319
00:20:45,261 --> 00:20:46,629
She gave them to us?!

320
00:20:46,829 --> 00:20:51,634
I first kidnapped that girl's mother
and then frightened her.

321
00:20:52,034 --> 00:20:54,436
It was easy to get her to listen then.

322
00:20:54,937 --> 00:20:56,572
What?!

323
00:20:58,140 --> 00:21:00,376
That's how it was...

324
00:21:02,945 --> 00:21:04,880
Where is Eri-san right now?!

325
00:21:05,414 --> 00:21:11,420
She's staying quietly aboard the yacht
"New Orient" anchored in Honmokufuto.

326
00:21:11,820 --> 00:21:13,489
She hasn't been hurt.

327
00:21:14,356 --> 00:21:18,193
About all she has is some seasickness.

328
00:21:22,698 --> 00:21:24,600
That's why Ran...

329
00:21:24,900 --> 00:21:28,637
Do you feel regret?
Isn't it vexing?

330
00:21:30,506 --> 00:21:32,341
This isn't regret.

331
00:21:32,441 --> 00:21:33,676
Huh?

332
00:21:35,344 --> 00:21:38,180
I'm pissed off like crazy!

333
00:21:40,482 --> 00:21:43,118
You took advantage of Ran's gentle heart...

334
00:21:43,686 --> 00:21:46,088
...you bastard!!

335
00:21:47,089 --> 00:21:48,624
Did you hear that?

336
00:21:49,191 --> 00:21:52,895
The "New Orient" in Honmokufuto.
Please hurry!

337
00:21:53,329 --> 00:21:54,463
What's that?!

338
00:21:56,598 --> 00:21:57,833
Don't move.

339
00:21:58,167 --> 00:21:59,935
What is this?

340
00:22:00,402 --> 00:22:03,439
Your wiretap uses radio waves.

341
00:22:03,605 --> 00:22:08,277
So I had Detective Sato and Detective Takagi
tap into those same radio waves.

342
00:22:09,645 --> 00:22:11,280
Since when...

343
00:22:11,714 --> 00:22:17,853
Kudo-kun ran by us in an all-to-obvious disguise
just as we had appeared at the police station.

344
00:22:18,120 --> 00:22:22,391
That's when I was certain he wanted
our secret cooperation in something.

345
00:22:22,491 --> 00:22:24,393
Once the two of them were inside...

346
00:22:24,560 --> 00:22:26,495
"Don't say a word, please meet us at the stairs."
...we made contact in the hallway.

347
00:22:27,296 --> 00:22:31,734
Where could Kisaki Eri-san be saved from?
Now the local police know.

348
00:22:32,201 --> 00:22:34,236
Damn...

349
00:22:41,310 --> 00:22:42,611
I'll press it!

350
00:22:42,678 --> 00:22:44,446
Fool! That's dangerous!

351
00:22:48,384 --> 00:22:51,720
Hirata Hajime! I arrest you on
suspicion of attempted murder.

352
00:22:56,058 --> 00:22:57,426
Ran!

353
00:23:00,095 --> 00:23:02,798
- Ran!
- Ran!

354
00:23:09,271 --> 00:23:10,672
Ran!

355
00:23:11,473 --> 00:23:13,242
Ran!

356
00:23:15,911 --> 00:23:18,647
Ran! Ran, hang in there!

357
00:23:19,248 --> 00:23:20,649
Ran...

358
00:23:20,749 --> 00:23:22,651
Ran, wake up.

359
00:23:25,888 --> 00:23:27,456
I...

360
00:23:32,828 --> 00:23:35,030
...wasn't in time?

361
00:23:37,766 --> 00:23:39,401
I...

362
00:23:41,403 --> 00:23:43,539
...wasn't in time?

363
00:24:01,590 --> 00:24:02,658
Ran?

364
00:24:12,601 --> 00:24:13,936
Ran...

365
00:24:17,706 --> 00:24:19,441
Shin'ichi?

366
00:24:27,316 --> 00:24:28,984
Are you crying?

367
00:24:32,254 --> 00:24:33,789
Fool.

368
00:24:34,723 --> 00:24:36,959
You're the one who's crying.

369
00:24:41,497 --> 00:24:43,298
Shin'ichi...

370
00:24:48,403 --> 00:24:50,205
I'm sorry...

371
00:24:52,941 --> 00:24:55,444
You're angry, aren't you?

372
00:25:01,717 --> 00:25:04,553
I'm so angry with myself, it's unbearable.

373
00:25:06,722 --> 00:25:11,059
That Ran was alone
all that time in the white room...

374
00:25:11,159 --> 00:25:13,262
...and troubled the entire time.

375
00:25:15,230 --> 00:25:18,200
And yet I never realized that.

376
00:25:22,304 --> 00:25:23,939
I'm truly...

377
00:25:25,440 --> 00:25:27,042
...very sorry.

378
00:25:30,078 --> 00:25:32,080
Shin'ichi...

379
00:25:38,854 --> 00:25:40,222
Still...

380
00:25:45,394 --> 00:25:47,796
I'm happy that you're safe.

381
00:25:59,341 --> 00:26:00,976
Dad...

382
00:26:04,079 --> 00:26:09,084
Dad, I'm sorry for worrying you, too.

383
00:26:09,351 --> 00:26:12,254
Ah, well... that's okay.

384
00:26:12,821 --> 00:26:15,657
All that matters is that you're safe.

385
00:26:17,392 --> 00:26:19,528
Eri's okay, too.

386
00:26:20,162 --> 00:26:22,497
Everything will be fine now.

387
00:26:23,865 --> 00:26:26,068
Everything's fine!

388
00:26:31,640 --> 00:26:35,811
Then I guess I'd better go see Eri.

389
00:26:44,019 --> 00:26:45,887
Thank goodness...

390
00:26:55,197 --> 00:26:58,800
Okay, let's get you to a hospital.

391
00:27:03,739 --> 00:27:05,641
Say, Shin'ichi.

392
00:27:05,741 --> 00:27:11,213
Being a detective; you can't do anything
other than track down criminals?

393
00:27:11,680 --> 00:27:12,881
I guess from here on, too...

394
00:27:12,948 --> 00:27:14,416
Yeah.

395
00:27:14,883 --> 00:27:17,552
I'll go on being a detective.

396
00:27:18,153 --> 00:27:23,692
I have to shoulder my responsibility as
a detective for each of the cases I solve.

397
00:27:24,593 --> 00:27:28,730
That's the thing I truly
came to understand today.

398
00:27:29,498 --> 00:27:31,166
I see...

399
00:27:31,400 --> 00:27:33,068
All right.

400
00:27:34,236 --> 00:27:36,338
Ahh!

401
00:27:36,705 --> 00:27:38,473
Since we were in that small place for so long...

402
00:27:38,573 --> 00:27:42,310
...once you leave the hospital,
let's go somewhere wide open and party.

403
00:27:42,444 --> 00:27:43,612
An amusement park!

404
00:27:43,679 --> 00:27:45,580
All right, all right.

405
00:27:45,814 --> 00:27:48,216
Then, once you've gotten all better...

406
00:27:48,383 --> 00:27:51,720
...and won the city Karate Convention
and recovered from that...

407
00:27:51,853 --> 00:27:53,255
...we'll go to an amusement park.

408
00:27:53,488 --> 00:27:54,723
All right!

409
00:27:54,756 --> 00:27:56,558
"Tropical Land"

410
00:27:56,692 --> 00:27:58,193
"Several Months Later"
Geez!

411
00:27:58,260 --> 00:28:01,229
I get invited out
by Shin'ichi and you run late.

412
00:28:01,363 --> 00:28:04,099
Sorry, sorry.
It's all my treat today.

413
00:28:05,133 --> 00:28:07,436
Can't be helped then.

414
00:28:07,703 --> 00:28:09,538
Ran, what do you want to ride?

415
00:28:09,604 --> 00:28:10,472
Of course it has to be...

416
00:28:10,539 --> 00:28:11,940
For pete's sake!

417
00:28:12,007 --> 00:28:15,644
I've been worried about them all this time
and they're out on a date?

418
00:28:15,977 --> 00:28:17,479
Well, whatever.

419
00:28:17,546 --> 00:28:19,748
No reason for me to interfere.

420
00:28:20,148 --> 00:28:21,516
Go!

421
00:28:22,651 --> 00:28:25,287
Ah, that's right, Ran.

422
00:28:26,088 --> 00:28:27,122
Here.

423
00:28:27,189 --> 00:28:29,858
"Like this, the case of
the white room was settled..."

424
00:28:30,025 --> 00:28:32,594
"...Ran was back to her normal cheerfulness..."

425
00:28:32,728 --> 00:28:36,798
"...and the two of us had come to
an amusement park to have fun."

426
00:28:37,165 --> 00:28:38,100
I'm so happy!

427
00:28:38,133 --> 00:28:41,636
"Truth is, it was there we would encounter
a shocking, big case..."

428
00:28:41,737 --> 00:28:47,075
"...and I would have an outrageous experience
with some mysterious men in black..."

429
00:28:47,275 --> 00:28:50,178
"Well, that's a story for another time."

430
00:28:50,378 --> 00:28:52,881
There is always just one truth!

431
00:28:52,914 --> 00:28:54,316
"This Drama Is Fictional"

